---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { updates } from "../data/updates";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Updates | CMNA"
  description="Corrections, software changes, teaching additions, and continuing work around Computational Methods for Numerical Analysis with R."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Living companion</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">What has changed since the book went to press.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        CMNA was published in 2017. Corrections, software, examples, and teaching
        material do not have to stop there. This page keeps those different kinds of
        change separate so a new laboratory does not masquerade as book errata.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two-column">
      <article class="content">
        <h2>Four kinds of change</h2>
        <p>
          A correction to the printed book, a new package release, a teaching note,
          and a new website feature are all useful, but they mean different things.
          The distinction matters. If a printed equation is wrong, a reader needs a
          correction. If the browser gets a new laboratory, the 2017 book did not
          suddenly become wrong.
        </p>
        <p>
          So this record uses explicit categories. Book errata correct or clarify the
          published text. Software entries record changes to the companion package.
          Teaching entries add material for instructors and students. Website entries
          describe the maintained companion itself.
        </p>

        <h2>No second edition is being announced</h2>
        <p>
          There is no second edition of CMNA at present. The site is useful on its own
          as a maintained companion to the existing book. If the accumulated work
          eventually supports another edition, there will be a much better record of
          what actually changed than a blank document and several years of memory.
        </p>
      </article>

      <aside class="updates-key">
        <h2>Categories</h2>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Book errata</dt><dd>Corrections or clarifications to the printed text.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Software</dt><dd>Released package changes and canonical source history.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Teaching</dt><dd>Course material, exercises, and instructor resources.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Website</dt><dd>Companion-site features and maintained examples.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section updates-section">
    <div class="shell updates-list">
      {updates.map((entry) => (
        <article class="update-entry">
          <div class="update-meta">
            <time datetime={entry.date}>{entry.date}</time>
            <span data-kind={entry.kind}>{entry.kind}</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2>{entry.title}</h2>
            <p>{entry.summary}</p>
            {entry.href && <a href={entry.href}>{entry.linkLabel ?? "More →"}</a>}
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
